                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04b8c30c-7983-38fa-93c1-6f16154c1843",
                        "entry_id": "d99451a0-c812-3121-b7a0-740ba941dd4f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "jemand, der Exegese (Auslegung, Deutung eines Textes) betreibt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8b4b709-e86a-4109-b014-77749e14e9b0",
                                "sense_id": "04b8c30c-7983-38fa-93c1-6f16154c1843",
                                "text": "„Exegeten des seltsamen Buchs halten für denkbar, dass das historische Schrifträtsel von einem Geisteskranken verfasst wurde.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3b1507b-c323-41ee-acc6-2f9170164b01",
                                "sense_id": "04b8c30c-7983-38fa-93c1-6f16154c1843",
                                "text": "„Ich bin kein Exeget.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3184028a-0a34-438b-8e76-e0cbb37dae5d",
                        "source_entry_id": "d99451a0-c812-3121-b7a0-740ba941dd4f",
                        "source_sense_id": "04b8c30c-7983-38fa-93c1-6f16154c1843",
                        "source_sense_description": "jemand, der Exegese (Auslegung, Deutung eines Textes) betreibt",
                        "target_lang_word": "exegete",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exegete",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "12cd5590-eef6-3ef3-9f31-8cd459ec24d3",
                                        "entry_id": "a4067827-2aa9-312a-bfcc-110f32ab6bfd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person skilled in exegesis; an interpreter of texts, difficult passages, law, oracles, and similar obscure or esoteric sources."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2ae46b8-4f62-4bd5-bba7-2e77a75683f7",
                                                "sense_id": "12cd5590-eef6-3ef3-9f31-8cd459ec24d3",
                                                "text": "A text that could not speak to the present was dead, and the exegete had a duty to revive it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1a1c391-fa39-42bb-851d-3bb759ada0e6",
                                                "sense_id": "12cd5590-eef6-3ef3-9f31-8cd459ec24d3",
                                                "text": "In Plato's state all three exegetes will be selected by Apollo. This is contrary to the practice of Hellenistic times, according to the evidence so ably marshaled by Oliver, when only two of the exegetes were named by the oracle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f2cbe8c-da73-41e2-a3ab-ec74cea37000",
                                                "sense_id": "12cd5590-eef6-3ef3-9f31-8cd459ec24d3",
                                                "text": "Theophrastus' \"superstitious man\" finds that a mouse has gnawed a hole in his meal sack and, obviously thinking it a portent, consults the exegete as to what he shall do... The exegete tells him, according to Theophrastus, to take the sack to a leather shop and have it mended. If this is drawn from life, it indicates that the exegetes discharged their functions with humour and common sense."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "exegete",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45b74457-1cae-3798-b1f1-966dd7466f3e",
                                        "entry_id": "6bfc9e1e-e3bc-3f8c-a981-7743b5cffd88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(chiefly religion) To interpret; to perform an exegesis on."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f47bc65-d12e-4f1b-9d54-0ee8c8420177",
                                                "sense_id": "45b74457-1cae-3798-b1f1-966dd7466f3e",
                                                "text": "History, not the dictionary, must exegete this doctrine. When thus exegeted, the secularity of our Government, as shown by the intentions of its founders, the customs of the people, and the continuous decisions of the courts, means simply the separation of church and state."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "da0f4a3f-c87c-4a79-ab36-96a4e0027a3d",
                        "source_entry_id": "d99451a0-c812-3121-b7a0-740ba941dd4f",
                        "source_sense_id": "04b8c30c-7983-38fa-93c1-6f16154c1843",
                        "source_sense_description": "jemand, der Exegese (Auslegung, Deutung eines Textes) betreibt",
                        "target_lang_word": "exegetist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exegetist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0c8c6eb-2a8f-33e9-9e64-11e6543b0d0c",
                                        "entry_id": "da817e34-51a6-3ac3-9e6d-280bed57f1ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person skilled in exegesis or interpretation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4af95c1a-d32c-40d7-9d13-f3612bd8db3a",
                        "source_entry_id": "d99451a0-c812-3121-b7a0-740ba941dd4f",
                        "source_sense_id": "04b8c30c-7983-38fa-93c1-6f16154c1843",
                        "source_sense_description": "jemand, der Exegese (Auslegung, Deutung eines Textes) betreibt",
                        "target_lang_word": "exégète",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exégète",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbca272f-4125-31a5-883b-a8ca58b14811",
                                        "entry_id": "7ff0377e-2daa-327c-a4d1-2d0268334474",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne qui s’occupe d’exégèse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9afe4359-63e7-4b13-b5c9-681f1adb0c0b",
                                                "sense_id": "dbca272f-4125-31a5-883b-a8ca58b14811",
                                                "text": "Où vous ne voyez qu’une phrase concrète et brutale, l’exégète voit un sens mystique dont la hauteur échappe à votre entendement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a259f334-fed7-48f0-a4da-a35e3c1db36f",
                                                "sense_id": "dbca272f-4125-31a5-883b-a8ca58b14811",
                                                "text": "Sieger dira qu’il énonce en exégète et non en théologien (enseigne à la faculté des arts, non de théologie), et que citer un auteur n’est pas reprendre à son compte l’énoncé."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6feecd8-2586-4ddc-9c34-9328c7189ec8",
                                                "sense_id": "dbca272f-4125-31a5-883b-a8ca58b14811",
                                                "text": "Aux exégètes amateurs qui comblent leurs lacunes par des préjugés et à ceux de mauvaise foi pour qui le soupçon tient lieu de raisonnement, il faut opposer une analyse dépassionnée du droit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1dbdbda6-9fb4-46cf-9aae-d58e1cac450b",
                                                "sense_id": "dbca272f-4125-31a5-883b-a8ca58b14811",
                                                "text": "Le lecteur contemporain se demandera, quant à lui, si le Réformateur n'est pas, sur ce point, pris en flagrant délit d’eiségèse. Plus généralement, il se demandera ce que pense de l’interprétation luthérienne de Paul un exégète professionnel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0828064-f05a-4ac6-9460-bd21640f41ad",
                                                "sense_id": "dbca272f-4125-31a5-883b-a8ca58b14811",
                                                "text": "« Awopbopaloobop alopbamboom » sera la première tentative de traduction de ce nouveau langage, qui ne repose pas sur des mots, mais sur une énergie fulgurante et créatrice. Little Richard parlait du « juste cri », Nik Cohn se fera l’exégète de sa glossolalie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
